# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo (see com.hakios.demo.plist).
# The Pixel 8a's vibration motor for Darwin (haptic=5: the CS40L26's RAM firmware is loaded ~50 s into the boot, so
# this waits first): the system's haptic feedbacks -- peek (1519), pop (1520), "nope" (1521) -- and the ringer's
# vibration (4095) as a program plays them; CoreHaptics' tap, vibration and taps; a long press on an icon (its menu),
# dismissed. The kernel's "akita haptic:" lines and the plug-in's "the actuator plays" say what came. RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.haptic3.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 60
/redwood/bin/sound_test springboard route
/redwood/bin/sound_test system 1519 wait 2 system 1520 wait 2 system 1521 wait 2 system 4095 wait 3
/redwood/bin/sound_test haptic wait 3
/redwood/bin/rwtouch hold 0.385 0.475 1200 wait 4 tap 0.5 0.2 wait 3
